Chapter: InductiveList

 The foreword's ordinary `List` cannot be inducted over. Stage 5 checks
 an induction by resolving the induction variable's type to a variant
 and generating one subgoal per constructor; `List` is a builtin whose
 elements are reached with `list-at` and `list-length` rather than a
 sum with `Nil` and `Cons` arms, so the resolution fails and the proof
 is accepted as an unproven axiom instead (CDX4022). That is honest --
 the compiler says so -- but it means `for all (xs : List Integer),
 5 === 6` compiles, and no property of a foreword container has ever
 been machine-checked. This chapter is the container that can be.

 It is deliberately NOT a replacement for `List`. `List` is the working
 collection: builtin, O(1) indexed, and what every other chapter takes
 and returns. `IList` is the shape you reach for when you intend to
 PROVE something, and `ilist-from-list` / `ilist-to-list` are the
 crossing between them. Reaching for it as a general-purpose list would
 trade an indexed structure for a linked one and gain nothing, because
 the proofs are compile-time only -- Stage 5 erases them at emit.

 Parametric rather than fixed to one element type, which was measured
 rather than assumed: Stage 5 walks `IList a` and checks a real claim
 over `IList Integer`, and a false one over the same type is a hard
 CDX2001 rather than a warning. `codex/test/reverse-reverse` had to
 declare its own `MyList` because no foreword container could be
 inducted over; `codex/test/inductive-list` proves the same flagship
 theorem over this one.

 We say:

Section: The Type

  IList a =
   | INil
   | ICons (a) (IList a)

Section: Construction

  ilist-append : IList a, IList a -> IList a
  ilist-append (xs) (ys) = when xs
   is INil -> ys
   is ICons (h) (t) -> ICons h (ilist-append t ys)

  ilist-reverse : IList a -> IList a
  ilist-reverse (xs) = when xs
   is INil -> INil
   is ICons (h) (t) -> ilist-append (ilist-reverse t) (ICons h INil)

  ilist-length : IList a -> Integer
  ilist-length (xs) = when xs
   is INil -> 0
   is ICons (h) (t) -> 1 + ilist-length t

Section: Crossing To And From List

  ilist-from-list : List a -> IList a
  ilist-from-list (xs) = ilist-from-list-loop xs (list-length xs - 1) INil

  ilist-from-list-loop : List a, Integer, IList a -> IList a
  ilist-from-list-loop (xs) (i) (acc) =
   if i < 0 then acc
   else ilist-from-list-loop xs (i - 1) (ICons (list-at xs i) acc)

  ilist-to-list : IList a -> List a
  ilist-to-list (xs) = ilist-to-list-loop xs []

  ilist-to-list-loop : IList a, List a -> List a
  ilist-to-list-loop (xs) (acc) = when xs
   is INil -> acc
   is ICons (h) (t) -> ilist-to-list-loop t (list-push acc h)
